Agent Commons includes reference modules from @uuaid/pillar by the UUAID project,
under Apache License 2.0.

Seven files come from the published @uuaid/pillar 2.0.2 package:
https://registry.npmjs.org/@uuaid/pillar/-/pillar-2.0.2.tgz

Three files (identity/keychain.mjs, net/envelope.mjs, net/refusals.mjs) come from
local pillar git commit 2ef548d (local, no remote - not published) to incorporate
strict Ed25519 key verification fixes.

Upstream project:
https://github.com/uuaid/pillar

The included reference modules provide Keychain, JCS, sealed envelope v2,
delegation verification, CarrierClient, tier definitions, seed-tier ranking,
refusal descriptions, and blob-size preflight helpers. Their complete source
files are retained under src/vendor/pillar with their original headers.
PROVENANCE.json pins each vendored file's SHA-256 and source origin.

Agent Commons does not claim to be an official Pillar release, an IAASO
certified implementation, or a replacement for every Pillar service feature.
The built-in Node SQLite carrier adapter is an Agent Commons implementation,
not a copy of the upstream native carrier, and exposes only its documented
capabilities. Libp2p, WebRTC, priority tier admission, blob brokering, and
public seed enrollment are not part of this adapter.
